    <Program class="ca.nrcan.gc.OEE.ERS.ErsProgram">
        <Labels>
            <English>EnerGuide Rating System</English>
            <French>Syst??????me de cote ??????nerGuide</French>
        </Labels>
        <Version major="15" minor="10" build="20288">
            <Labels>
                <English>v15.10b20288</English>
                <French>v15.10b20288</French>
            </Labels>
        </Version>
        <SdkVersion major="1" minor="16" build="20288">
            <Labels>
                <English>v1.16b20288</English>
                <French>v1.16b20288</French>
            </Labels>
        </SdkVersion>
        <Options>
            <Main applyHouseholdOperatingConditions="false" applyReducedOperatingConditions="false" atypicalElectricalLoads="false" waterConservation="true" referenceHouse="false">
                <Vermiculite code="3">
                    <English>No Vermiculite</English>
                    <French>Pas de Vermiculite</French>
                </Vermiculite>
            </Main>
            <WaterConservation LowFlushToilets="3" LowFlushToiletsUpgrade="0" />
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>The infiltration test has shown air leakage from the following house components:

- Receptacles

- Header joist

- All windows

- All exterior doors

- All bathroom fans

- Fireplace

- Wood stove chimney

During the infiltration test walkthrough, we notice air leakage on the items listed above. Airtightness is very important to achieve energy savings.

</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>At the time of the assessment, the insulation of the exterior walls was R-12. We recommend upgrading the insulation level. You are eligible for $2.50/square inch for the addition of R-20+,  and $ 3.50/square inch for R-30+. The insulation will help you to increase the airtightness of your home and contribute to energy savings.</mainWalls>
                <ceilingsCathedral>At the time of the audit, the attic insulation inspection was estimated to R-20. We recommend adding insulation to meet the city of Whitehorse standard of R-60. </ceilingsCathedral>
                <windows>We recommend the replacement of the windows by triple pane and Energy Star certified units with Lowe coating and Argon filled.</windows>
                <doors>We recommend the replacement of all doors by new energy star certified products.  </doors>
                <VentilationSystem>The result of the infiltration test has shown that your house's natural air exchange is not enough. We recommend the installation of an HRV (Heat Recovery Ventilator) HVI (Home Ventilation Institute) and Energy Star certified, to ensure proper ventilation inside your home.</VentilationSystem>
                <HeatingSystem> Changing the heating system is a big decision and it?????????s not easy to choose. To help you decide we suggest the following points:

- Source of energy

- Efficiency

- Maintenance

- Cost (To acquire the system and maintenance)

- Your comfort



Have you already thought about having a heat pump. This type of heating system can use up to 3 times less energy than a typical baseboard and needs electricity to operate. However this kind of system can?????????t operate on temperature below -25 degrees celcius, it then will require a secondary system to maintain the heat. In this case, the furnace can ensure the heat and the ducting system can be used by the heat pump to supply heat in the entire building. You might be eligible to participate in the Heat Pumps pilot project, please follow the link below for more information;

https://yukon.ca/en/news/expanded-rebates-renewable-home-heating-now-available



</HeatingSystem>
                <Renewables>For any questions concerning the rebates and the programs about solar energy, please follow the link below to get more information:

https://yukon.ca/en/renewable-energy-rebate#eligible-renewable-systems



</Renewables>
                <AdditionalComments>For more information concerning the Electrical Thermal Storage Unit, please follow the link below:

http://yukonconservation.org/programs/energy/electric-thermal-storage#:~:text=Electric%20thermal%20storage%20(ETS)%20is,providing%20heat%20throughout%20the%20day  

</AdditionalComments>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
